You’re very close—just a couple of method name + terminal operation issues.

**Fixed version (Java 8):**
```java
import java.util.*;
import java.util.stream.*;

public class Test {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int[] arr = {1,2,5,3,8,4,9,6,7};

        int[] sorted = Arrays.stream(arr)
                             .sorted()
                             .toArray();

        System.out.println(Arrays.toString(sorted));
    }
}
```

**If you want List instead:**
```java
List<Integer> list = Arrays.stream(arr)
                           .boxed()
                           .sorted()
                           .collect(Collectors.toList());
```

**In-place sort (simplest):**
```java
Arrays.sort(arr);
```

बस mistake ये थी:
- `streams()` ❌ → `stream()` ✅  
- `sort()` ❌ → `sorted()` ✅  
- `collect()` ❌ (primitive stream) → `toArray()` ✅

please correct

import java.util.*;
import java.util.stream.*;

public class Test {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int[] arr = {1,2,5,3,8,4,9,6,7};

        int[] sorted = Arrays.stream(arr)
                             .sorted(Comparator.reversed())
                             .toArray();

        System.out.println(Arrays.toString(sorted));
    }
}

`IntStream` pe `Comparator` apply nahi hota—pehle `boxed()` karo.

**Correct code (descending):**
```java id="x8k2az"
import java.util.*;
import java.util.stream.*;

public class Test {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int[] arr = {1,2,5,3,8,4,9,6,7};

        int[] sorted = Arrays.stream(arr)
                             .boxed()
                             .sorted(Comparator.reverseOrder())
                             .mapToInt(Integer::intValue)
                             .toArray();

        System.out.println(Arrays.toString(sorted));
    }
}
```

**Short trick (no boxing):**
```java id="r3m91p"
int[] sorted = Arrays.stream(arr)
                     .map(x -> -x)
                     .sorted()
                     .map(x -> -x)
                     .toArray();
