## ✅ 2️⃣ Using `CompletableFuture` (chained loop)
```java
import java.util.concurrent.CompletableFuture;
import java.util.concurrent.ExecutorService;
import java.util.concurrent.Executors;

class ABCCompletableFuture {

    private final ExecutorService executor = Executors.newFixedThreadPool(3);

    public void start() {
        CompletableFuture<Void> future = CompletableFuture.completedFuture(null);

        while (true) {
            future = future
                    .thenRunAsync(() -> System.out.print("A"), executor)
                    .thenRunAsync(() -> System.out.print("B"), executor)
                    .thenRunAsync(() -> System.out.print("C"), executor);
        }
    }
}
```

### ▶️ Run
```java
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        new ABCCompletableFuture().start();
    }
}
```

